                    {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "text": "Two important characteristics of DBMSs are data independence, which guarantees that modifications to data structures do not impact application layers, and data abstraction, which makes database interactions simpler by shielding users from the complexity of data storage. Additionally, it provides concurrency control, which permits several users to access data concurrently and peacefully"
