                    {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "text": "A file system and a DBMS are two kinds of data management systems that are used in different capacities and possess different characteristics. A File System is a way of organizing files into groups and folders and then storing them in a storage device. It provides the media that stores data as well as enables users to perform procedures such as reading, writing, and even erasure."
