                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "text": "File systems are used to manage files and directories, and provide basic operations for creating, deleting, renaming, and accessing files. They typically store data in a hierarchical structure, where files are organized in directories and subdirectories. File systems are simple and efficient, but they lack the ability to manage complex data relationships and ensure data consistency."
