                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "text": "On the other hand, DBMS is a software system designed to manage large amounts of structured data, and provide advanced operations for storing, retrieving, and manipulating data. DBMS provides a centralized and organized way of storing data, which can be accessed and modified by multiple users or applications. DBMS offers advanced features like data validation, indexing , transactions, concurrency control , and backup and recovery mechanisms. DBMS ensures data consistency, accuracy, and integrity by enforcing data constraints, such as primary keys, foreign keys, and data types."
                    },
